  "english": "Friday: Patristic [Harts] of Rest.\nAt the Midday Liturgy:\nPsalm 97 [98]: \"All [the ends of the earth] have seen.\"\nApostle: 2 Corinthians 10:7 \"Brethren, look at what is before your eyes...\" to verse 17 \"...let him boast in the Lord.\"\nAlleluia: according to the tone [of the day].\nGospel: Mark 9:37 [Armenian 9:38] \"John said to him...\" to verse 49 [Armenian 9:50] \"...be at peace with one another.\"\n[Tone 1st Side / Ayb-Dza]\n\nSaturday: Feast of the Holy Church for the Dedication [Navakatik] of the Holy Cross.\nMorning Hymn [Arakyn] Tone 2nd Side [b-k]: \"Upon the rock of faith,\" with its proper canon [sarokn].\nMagnificat [Metsatsustse] Tone 1st Side [a-dz]: \"We magnify.\"\nSong: \"Holiness befits your house.\"\nLitany: \"Let us say.\"\n\"Holy God,\" who wast crucified.\nAt the Fellowship [Mankunk] Hymn Tone 2nd Side [a-k]: \"Your altar, O Lord.\"\nAfter the Fellowship [Mankunk]: Litany \"By the Holy Church,\" [then] \"Save [us].\"\nPrayer: \"At the door of this holy temple.\"\nAt the Midday Liturgy, Introit: \"In peace.\"\nAntiphon: \"The Lord reigns.\"\nHymn Tone 2nd Side [a-k]: \"Your altar, O Lord.\"\nPsalm 64 [65]: \"Praise is due to you.\"\nProverbs 3:9 \"Honor the Lord...\" to verse 17 \"...in peace.\"\nProphet Isaiah 66:12 \"For thus says the Lord...\" to verse 16 \"...all flesh.\"\nApostle 1 Timothy 3:14 \"I am writing these things...\" to verse 16 \"...taken up in glory.\"\nAlleluia: \"O Lord, I love [the beauty of your house].\"\nGospel John 10:22 \"At that time the Feast of Dedication took place...\" to verse 42 \"...and many believed in him there.\"\nHymn of the Great Entrance [Srbasatsutiun]: \"Angelic.\"\nIn the Evening: \"Gladsome Light.\"\nMessedi: \"Bless the Lord, all you servants.\"\nLitany: \"Let us say.\"\nAnd the priests shall vest together and come out to the chancel with the cross and gospel book and all adornments.\n\"Holy God,\" who wast crucified.\nHymn at Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 1st Side [a-dz]: \"Who [spreadest] your immaculate arms.\"\nLitany: \"By your holy cross,\" [then] \"Save [us].\"\nPrayer: \"Guard us [O Christ our God].\"\nHymn of the Great Entrance [Srbasatsutiun]: \"Multitudes of.\"\nIn the Evening, Messedi: \"My soul magnifies.\"\nLitany: \"Holy Mother.\"\nHymn at Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 4th Side [d-g]: \"A new Zion is born.\"\nAfterward, Litany: \"Holy Mother of God,\" [then] \"Save [us].\"\nPrayer: \"Receive, O Lord, our supplications.\"\n\nAnd then the Fast of the Holy Cross, during which there are no feasts.\n\nMonday of the Fast: Patristic [Harts] of Repentance.\nAt the Midday Liturgy:\nPsalm 144 [145]: \"Your kingdom.\"\nApostle: 2 Corinthians 8:1 \"We want you to know...\" to verse 15 \"...had nothing left over.\"\nAlleluia: \"Come, let us sing.\"\nGospel: Mark 8:1 \"In those days...\" to verse 9 \"...and he sent them away.\"\n\nTuesday: Patristic [Harts] of Repentance.\nAt the Midday Liturgy:\nPsalm 5: \"I will bow down.\"\nApostle: 2 Corinthians 8:16 \"But thanks be...\" to verse 24 \"...of the churches.\"\nAlleluia: \"Sing to the Lord.\"\nGospel: Mark 8:10 \"And immediately...\" to verse 21 \"...Do you not yet understand?\"\n\nWednesday: Patristic [Harts] of Repentance.\nAt the Midday Liturgy:\nPsalm 85 [86]: \"Save your servant.\"\nApostle: 2 Corinthians 9:1 \"Now it is superfluous...\" to verse 9 \"...endures forever.\"\nAlleluia: according to the tone [of the day].\nGospel: Mark 8:22 [Armenian 8:23] \"And they came to Bethsaida...\" to verse 26 \"Do not even enter the village.\"\n\nThursday: Patristic [Harts] of Repentance.\nAt the Midday Liturgy:\nPsalm 98 [99]: \"Extol [the Lord].\"\nApostle: 2 Corinthians 9:10 \"He who supplies...\" to [Chapter 10] verse 6 \"...is complete.\"\nAlleluia: \"Extol [the Lord].\"\nGospel: Mark 9:13 [Armenian 9:14] \"And when they came...\" to verse 26 [Armenian 9:27] \"...and he stood up.\"",
